{
  "about": [
    "Shared vectors for the listing of a screen library: the list, its digest and the refusals.",
    "Authored in canopy (tests/canopy_mcp/fixtures/listing-vectors.json); every other holder keeps a byte-identical copy.",
    "ASCII-only: other characters are spelled as \\u escapes, a lone surrogate included. No trailing whitespace, one final newline.",
    "Each case is a list of entries as a scan of a library root reports them and what the pure judge makes of them; no case touches a filesystem, because a case-insensitive host cannot hold two names that differ only in case.",
    "An entry is {path, kind, mode, sha256}: path relative to the root with '/', kind one of file, dir, symlink, other (from lstat), mode the permission bits, sha256 on files only. The judge reads path, kind and sha256.",
    "list is the text of the list: one line '<sha256>  screens/<relpath>' plus LF per listed file, sorted by the UTF-8 bytes of relpath. digest is 'sha256:' plus the hex sha256 of the UTF-8 bytes of list.",
    "A file is listed when it is a regular file under screens/ named *.screen.json (as spelled) or carrying an image suffix (in any case: .png .jpg .jpeg .gif .svg .webp .bmp .ico) and no segment of its path below screens/ is refused.",
    "refusals are {path, code}, sorted by the UTF-8 bytes of path (a lone surrogate encoded as such), then code. Codes: outside_screens (reported once, at the top-level name; LIBRARY-REPORT.json and LIBRARY-REPORT.md are the only files allowed beside screens/), symlink, not_regular, bad_name (a character of category Cc, Cf or Cs), leftover_tmp ('.' ... '.tmp', below screens/ or as an entry of the root itself), dotfile, ignored_name, suffix, case_collision.",
    "A name rule (bad_name, leftover_tmp, dotfile, ignored_name; the first that applies, in that order) is judged on every segment below screens/ and reported at the shortest path that breaks it; an entry under a refused name earns no refusal of its own. Otherwise the kind decides: symlink, not_regular, or for a file its suffix.",
    "A regular file named exactly .DS_Store is skipped anywhere: neither listed nor refused.",
    "case_collision names every spelling, among the entries below screens/ and their directory prefixes, that shares its str.casefold() with a different spelling. A colliding file is still listed.",
    "ignoredNames pins the name predicate behind ignored_name and dotfile: a name starting with '.', the name __pycache__, the configuredIgnoredNames, and the endings .swp .swo .pyc .pyo .pyd .log .pid, each compared on name.casefold(). Every case is judged with configuredIgnoredNames as the deployment's own ignored names (CANOPY_LIBRARY_IGNORED_NAMES)."
  ],
  "configuredIgnoredNames": [
    "claude.local.md",
    "dockerfile",
    "prefetched-models",
    "var"
  ],
  "ignoredNames": {
    "refused": [
      ".env",
      ".env.shared",
      ".venv",
      ".git",
      "var",
      "VAR",
      "__pycache__",
      "x.pyc",
      "x.pyo",
      "x.pyd",
      ".pytest_cache",
      "a.log",
      "A.LOG",
      "a.pid",
      ".DS_Store",
      ".claude",
      "CLAUDE.local.md",
      "claude.LOCAL.md",
      "Dockerfile",
      "dockerfile",
      "prefetched-models",
      "a.swp",
      "a.swo"
    ],
    "accepted": [
      "a.screen.json",
      "variant",
      "log",
      "-a",
      "dockerfile.png",
      "models",
      "a.py",
      "a.logs"
    ]
  },
